# Agents that wake themselves

```elixir
Mix.install([{:wardrik, "~> 0.1.0-rc.7"}, {:kino, "~> 0.19"}])
```

## Setup

An agent wakes every minute, and when a signed webhook arrives. Add `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in the
Secrets panel. Ten minutes of it costs about a cent.

`:vault_keys` seals the webhook's secret. Keep yours in config, not code.

```elixir
System.put_env("ANTHROPIC_API_KEY", System.fetch_env!("LB_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"))

defmodule MyApp.AllowAll do
  @behaviour Wardrik.Authorizer
  def authorize(_request, _opts), do: :ok
end

defmodule MyApp.Agents do
  @behaviour Wardrik.Resolver
  def resolve(_request, _opts), do: {:ok, %Wardrik.Resolved{principal: Wardrik.principal("maria")}}
end

{:ok, _} =
  Wardrik.start_link(
    name: MyApp.AgentRuntime,
    authorizer: {MyApp.AllowAll, []},
    resolver: {MyApp.Agents, []},
    vault_keys: [WardrikVault.generate_key()]
  )

scope = Wardrik.as(MyApp.AgentRuntime, "maria")

# A Standard Webhooks secret, sealed for Maria.
hook_secret = "whsec_" <> Base.encode64(:crypto.strong_rand_bytes(24))

{:ok, _vsn} =
  WardrikVault.put(
    MyApp.AgentRuntime.Vault,
    %WardrikVault.Secret{principal: Wardrik.principal("maria"), name: "ORDERS_HOOK", value: hook_secret},
    kind: :signing_secret
  )
```

## The agent

```elixir
{:ok, agent} =
  Wardrik.Agent.define(scope, "agt_watcher",
    model: "anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5",
    instructions: "You watch Acme's orders. Answer in one short line.",
    policy: [budget: [usd: 0.25, per: :day]],
    triggers: [
      %{name: "heartbeat", every: "1m", prompt: "Say you're awake and watching."},
      %{
        name: "orders",
        webhook: %{secret: "${ORDERS_HOOK}", verify: "standard"},
        prompt: "A new order came in. Summarise it."
      }
    ]
  )

agent.next_run
```

## Watch it wake

```elixir
woke = fn ->
  {:ok, page} = Wardrik.Agent.events(scope, agent, types: ["wardrik.trigger.fired"])

  for event <- page.events,
      do: %{time: event.time, trigger: event.data["trigger"]["name"], status: event.data["status"]}
end

Kino.animate(2000, fn _tick ->
  Kino.DataTable.new(woke.(), keys: [:time, :trigger, :status], name: "What woke it")
end)
```

`asked` means it asked the agent. `busy` means the agent was still working, so it skipped.

## Send a webhook

The notebook plays the service. It signs the body and delivers it, as
`POST /v1/hooks/agt_watcher/orders` would:

```elixir
sign = fn body ->
  "whsec_" <> key = hook_secret
  id = "msg_" <> Base.url_encode64(:crypto.strong_rand_bytes(9))
  timestamp = Integer.to_string(System.os_time(:second))
  signature = :crypto.mac(:hmac, :sha256, Base.decode64!(key), "#{id}.#{timestamp}.#{body}")

  %{
    "webhook-id" => id,
    "webhook-timestamp" => timestamp,
    "webhook-signature" => "v1," <> Base.encode64(signature)
  }
end

body = ~s({"order": "A-3", "customer": "Initech", "total": "$1,240.00"})
headers = sign.(body)

Wardrik.Hook.deliver(scope, agent: agent, trigger: "orders", body: body, headers: headers)
```

A changed body fails the signature, and returns `not_found`:

```elixir
Wardrik.Hook.deliver(scope, agent: agent, trigger: "orders", body: ~s({"total": "$1"}), headers: headers)
```

## Change and remove

```elixir
Wardrik.Agent.trigger_set(scope, agent: agent, trigger: "heartbeat", every: "2m", prompt: "Still awake?")
```

```elixir
Wardrik.Agent.trigger_remove(scope, agent: agent, trigger: "heartbeat")
```

